WEBVTT

00:01.960 --> 00:06.005
Look, guys! I found 500 yen
under a vending machine.

00:06.089 --> 00:08.341
Thought I'd get something yummy
for Piisuke and me…

00:10.176 --> 00:13.638
I wanted to tell everyone
about Bring Your Parents to School Day,

00:13.722 --> 00:17.517
but Daddy and Shin and Lu, they all left!

00:20.687 --> 00:21.521
Don't cry.

00:21.604 --> 00:25.316
Here, you want some acorns?
I have candy too.

00:30.405 --> 00:33.742
Tell ya what, I'll go find them for you.

00:35.285 --> 00:36.703
Really?

00:39.289 --> 00:41.332
You know what to do, Piisuke!

00:43.293 --> 00:44.961
BASEMENT LEVEL FOUR

00:46.045 --> 00:47.547
Who are you, old man?

00:48.131 --> 00:50.842
I'm Asakura, the director of this place.

00:50.925 --> 00:54.054
Could I interest you two
in a little prison break?

00:54.137 --> 00:56.181
The director?

00:57.223 --> 00:58.099
So that means…

00:59.851 --> 01:02.353
you're the one behind my kidnapping!

01:02.437 --> 01:04.230
No, no! I'm not!

01:04.314 --> 01:06.399
If I were, why would I be
stuck in here with you?

01:07.192 --> 01:08.318
Right, good point.

01:08.860 --> 01:11.905
Fine. Then tell me everything you know!

02:44.330 --> 02:45.957
SAKAMOTO'S VS THE LAB

02:46.040 --> 02:49.794
You must be the legendary hit man,
Taro Sakamoto.

02:49.878 --> 02:53.214
That power and speed? Impressive.

02:53.298 --> 02:55.884
But I gotta say,
you gotta lose some weight!

02:55.967 --> 02:58.011
Even I was able to beat you to the draw.

02:59.679 --> 03:03.141
Let's see what happens next, shall we?

03:03.725 --> 03:04.726
It won't matter.

03:08.271 --> 03:10.773
WHY ME, MR. SAKAMOTO?

03:13.693 --> 03:16.613
I meant to hit the enemy,
yet my body moved on its own.

03:17.906 --> 03:19.824
That needle in your neck, Sakamoto,

03:19.908 --> 03:24.829
transmits a signal that makes your brain
confuse your friends for foes.

03:25.330 --> 03:26.289
Neat, isn't--

03:28.833 --> 03:32.086
Then that means
I just need to try to attack Shin.

03:32.170 --> 03:33.004
WAIT…

03:33.087 --> 03:35.840
<i>Why was his punch so much stronger</i>
<i>when it was meant for me?!</i>

03:36.841 --> 03:38.343
I must say…

03:41.012 --> 03:42.889
I like a feisty little guinea pig.

03:45.558 --> 03:46.601
And so,

03:46.684 --> 03:51.064
since I didn't follow their orders,
they locked me up in this cell.

03:51.147 --> 03:51.981
The end.

03:52.065 --> 03:55.985
Then what do they want with me?
Your story's too complicated, old man.

03:56.069 --> 03:57.946
How should I know? I don't know you!

03:58.905 --> 04:00.448
Come to think of it,

04:00.531 --> 04:04.744
this all started because
you mistook me for Shin and kidnapped me!

04:04.827 --> 04:08.248
Shin? Do you mean Shin the psychic?

04:08.831 --> 04:10.750
You know him?

04:10.833 --> 04:12.752
Know him?

04:12.835 --> 04:16.756
I'm the one responsible
for making him psychic.

04:16.839 --> 04:20.677
What? I thought Shin
was born with that power.

04:21.302 --> 04:24.347
He used to be a plain-old brat.

04:25.556 --> 04:28.017
It's my fault that his life
changed forever.

04:28.643 --> 04:30.436
I got him mixed up in my research.

04:31.062 --> 04:34.315
Meat is hard and rubbery. I don't like it!

04:37.235 --> 04:39.279
I'm not wasting good nutrition
on a dummy like you.

04:39.362 --> 04:43.074
The magnesium in meat
lowers the risk of malnourishment.

04:43.157 --> 04:44.951
Keep that in mind, you brat!

04:45.034 --> 04:47.954
I don't need to eat that,
I can just drink my juice!

04:49.247 --> 04:52.041
<i>Why do I have to babysit this brat?</i>

04:52.125 --> 04:53.251
MIKAN JUICE

04:56.504 --> 05:00.174
<i>Back then, I was doing research</i>
<i>on supernatural abilities at the Lab.</i>

05:00.883 --> 05:01.926
<i>One day,</i>

05:02.510 --> 05:05.888
<i>an old friend of mine named Ando</i>
<i>asked me to take care of Shin</i>

05:05.972 --> 05:07.473
<i>and vanished into thin air.</i>

05:11.477 --> 05:13.396
That's my special smoothie!

05:17.442 --> 05:19.944
Damn it. Nothing's working…

05:20.028 --> 05:22.280
Old man, whatcha doing there?

05:22.947 --> 05:27.201
Well, I'm researching how to expand
the limits of human brain activity.

05:29.454 --> 05:32.248
Simply put,
I'm studying supernatural powers.

05:32.790 --> 05:34.625
Is that fun?

05:34.709 --> 05:37.712
Are you crazy? There's nothing better.

05:38.254 --> 05:39.589
If I figure it out,

05:39.672 --> 05:43.468
we might be able to unlock
incredible potential for humankind.

05:44.343 --> 05:46.220
Potential for humankind?

05:46.304 --> 05:47.555
That's right.

05:47.638 --> 05:51.184
It means I might be able to make
everybody super happy.

06:13.414 --> 06:15.917
Look at him. He looks drained.

06:16.000 --> 06:18.461
Hell-bent on research that won't work?

06:18.544 --> 06:20.463
Wish I had that kind of time to waste.

06:21.047 --> 06:23.299
You don't know it won't work!

06:24.383 --> 06:28.888
The old man's working hard
to make everybody super happy.

06:33.059 --> 06:35.186
I've never seen anything like this!

06:35.269 --> 06:39.107
I have to compare it with previous data.

06:39.982 --> 06:41.859
I'm thirsty.

06:42.527 --> 06:45.822
It worked! It really worked!

06:45.905 --> 06:47.198
Shin, I did it!

06:48.574 --> 06:51.035
What are you doing?!

06:51.119 --> 06:52.370
What do you mean?

06:53.287 --> 06:55.873
Are you all right, Shin?

06:57.333 --> 06:58.709
That was nasty!

07:01.462 --> 07:02.672
<i>I don't see any change.</i>

07:03.339 --> 07:04.298
<i>I guess it failed.</i>

07:05.007 --> 07:07.927
<i>But at least that means he's okay.</i>

07:08.010 --> 07:09.720
I'm not okay!

07:09.804 --> 07:12.723
That stuff tasted really bad!

07:12.807 --> 07:16.352
What? Was I speaking out loud?

07:16.936 --> 07:18.312
Mr. Tada, you were just thinking,

07:18.396 --> 07:21.107
"I wish I could see Ms. Namiki's panties,"
weren't you?

07:21.190 --> 07:22.567
-What?
-Hey!

07:23.693 --> 07:27.113
Oh, Ms. Namiki thinks you're a creep.

07:32.743 --> 07:33.578
Poop!

07:34.078 --> 07:35.288
Star!

07:35.371 --> 07:36.205
Toupee!

07:36.831 --> 07:39.000
Hey, guys, let's play.

07:39.083 --> 07:40.877
I'm a bit busy right now.

07:40.960 --> 07:41.878
Maybe later.

07:41.961 --> 07:42.879
Sorry, kid.

07:44.714 --> 07:45.548
Phooey.

07:47.967 --> 07:50.178
<i>-I don't want to be near him.</i>
<i>-It's freaky.</i>

07:50.261 --> 07:51.512
<i>What an annoying power.</i>

07:51.596 --> 07:54.891
<i>-I feel sorry for him, but it's creepy.</i>
<i>-Poor Shin.</i>

07:55.475 --> 07:56.893
Don't worry, Shin.

07:56.976 --> 07:59.604
I'll make a cure that'll fix it all.

07:59.687 --> 08:01.022
I'm fine like this!

08:01.689 --> 08:04.317
It finally worked. Aren't you happy?

08:05.067 --> 08:06.110
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

08:06.694 --> 08:09.906
<i>I'm sorry that I got you tangled up</i>
<i>in my stupid research.</i>

08:10.656 --> 08:12.909
Your research isn't stupid!

08:13.868 --> 08:15.244
Forget it!

08:16.829 --> 08:20.124
The guys at the Lab are boring,
and you're a gloomy old man now.

08:20.625 --> 08:22.168
You suck!

08:25.338 --> 08:28.257
A little while after that, he left.

08:29.091 --> 08:31.260
I don't know how I could ever face him.

08:33.888 --> 08:35.765
What a sad story.

08:36.849 --> 08:39.393
But I bet Shin isn't mad anymore.

08:39.477 --> 08:40.603
Why do you think so?

08:41.604 --> 08:44.148
I'm with him every day. I can tell!

08:44.899 --> 08:46.817
Shin's happy with his power.

08:46.901 --> 08:50.029
And our manager doesn't talk much,
so I'm jealous.

08:50.112 --> 08:51.030
Manager?

08:51.531 --> 08:53.950
Why don't you apologize with me, old guy?

08:54.450 --> 08:57.036
I actually had a fight with Shin too.

08:57.787 --> 09:00.039
Sakamoto family rule number 11.

09:00.540 --> 09:02.959
"If you fight, make peace the same day."

09:03.042 --> 09:05.378
You're a bit late for the "same day" part,

09:05.461 --> 09:07.338
but you can bribe him with sweets!

09:09.882 --> 09:12.093
I feel like a fool for sulking.

09:16.847 --> 09:19.850
If you had this,
why didn't you break out sooner?

09:19.934 --> 09:23.854
As long as I'm in here,
I don't have to help with their research.

09:25.147 --> 09:26.065
Little lady,

09:26.732 --> 09:28.442
has he grown taller?

09:32.488 --> 09:33.322
Who's there?

09:45.585 --> 09:48.170
You're gonna have to see for yourself,
old guy.

09:49.297 --> 09:52.300
Ready? Commence escape mission!

09:54.719 --> 09:55.553
WHY ME?

09:57.263 --> 09:59.015
Hmm? Sorry.

09:59.098 --> 10:00.016
Isn't it great?

10:00.600 --> 10:02.893
This switch can turn it on and off.

10:03.603 --> 10:05.688
What else do I have?

10:05.771 --> 10:08.649
Hang on… Let's see…

10:08.733 --> 10:09.567
YIKES!

10:09.650 --> 10:12.737
<i>-So cringey.</i>
-Look at what I can do!

10:15.323 --> 10:17.074
You don't learn, do you?

10:19.744 --> 10:21.162
<i>Nice kick.</i>

10:21.245 --> 10:22.788
THANK YOU, SIR…

10:23.456 --> 10:24.624
And click!

10:27.043 --> 10:27.877
ARGH!

10:29.587 --> 10:33.424
Whoopsie-daisy. He was so light,
I tossed him right through the glass.

10:35.468 --> 10:36.802
It won't work.

10:39.055 --> 10:41.265
With your brain mistaking me as a friend,

10:41.349 --> 10:43.559
your hand freezes on reflex, doesn't it?

10:43.643 --> 10:48.189
Even the legendary hit man is no match
for the magnificent power of science.

10:48.522 --> 10:51.067
IF I READ YOUR MIND, THAT WON'T MATTER.

10:56.364 --> 10:57.198
AH!

10:58.282 --> 10:59.825
Read my mind all you want.

10:59.909 --> 11:02.203
It won't matter
if your body can't keep up.

11:03.287 --> 11:07.083
My golly, I have no clue
why the boss would want

11:07.166 --> 11:09.168
such a stupid power like yours.

11:12.630 --> 11:13.798
It's stupid!

11:13.881 --> 11:17.134
It's so uninspired. I couldn't care less!

11:18.344 --> 11:20.012
STUPID? HOW DARE YOU…

11:22.056 --> 11:25.309
Don't get your clothes too dirty.
It'll be a hassle to wash.

11:27.061 --> 11:30.815
Also, his power isn't stupid at all.

11:31.440 --> 11:33.234
And I can prove it to you.

11:34.193 --> 11:35.236
MR. SAKAMOTO…

11:37.029 --> 11:41.659
There's such a big gap in our IQs
that I can't even converse with you.

11:42.326 --> 11:43.244
Time to kill you!

11:47.081 --> 11:50.501
Oh, that feels good!

11:51.085 --> 11:52.878
WHAT ARE WE GONNA DO, MR. SAKAMOTO?

11:53.712 --> 11:55.089
<i>It's simple.</i>

11:55.172 --> 11:56.006
HUH?

11:57.967 --> 11:58.884
SERIOUSLY?

11:59.593 --> 12:02.221
Let's begin the final experiment.

12:02.304 --> 12:03.139
Huh?

12:11.564 --> 12:13.899
Are you taunting me?

12:13.983 --> 12:15.234
<i>Straight right.</i>

12:17.027 --> 12:19.447
<i>Left hook, straight right,</i>
<i>left roundhouse, right uppercut,</i>

12:19.530 --> 12:21.574
<i>straight right, straight left,</i>
<i>right jab, left jab,</i>

12:21.657 --> 12:23.576
<i>right roundhouse, left roundhouse…</i>

12:23.659 --> 12:27.455
<i>How's the kid avoiding it all?</i>
<i>How is he aiming at me?</i>

12:28.164 --> 12:31.167
<i>Sakamoto must be telling him his moves</i>
<i>by thinking them.</i>

12:32.501 --> 12:33.335
You pesky…

12:33.919 --> 12:36.088
humanities majors!

12:37.923 --> 12:41.844
Oh, that feels good!

12:45.973 --> 12:47.600
<i>I thought I was gonna die!</i>

12:49.101 --> 12:52.021
LEADER, MAD HORIGUCHI
THROWING IN THE TOWEL

12:52.980 --> 12:54.148
Hold still.

12:55.608 --> 12:57.109
There you go.

12:57.193 --> 12:58.027
Thank you.

12:59.236 --> 13:00.863
Thanks, Shin.

13:02.615 --> 13:04.783
We need to apologize to you.

13:05.784 --> 13:08.037
Nah, don't worry about it.

13:08.996 --> 13:13.667
I'm happy with this power
and I'm happy with where I am now.

13:14.335 --> 13:16.879
Oh yeah? Glad to see you're doing well.

13:16.962 --> 13:21.050
I work at Mr. Sakamoto's shop now.

13:21.550 --> 13:23.677
I've got mad cashier skills, too.

13:24.261 --> 13:26.180
Thank you for taking care of Shin.

13:26.263 --> 13:27.097
Sure.

13:27.973 --> 13:30.893
I know you've been out of the game
for a while now,

13:30.976 --> 13:34.396
but I'm still pretty stoked
that I was able to dodge all your attacks.

13:34.480 --> 13:36.941
You're fat now, so it felt more intense--

13:40.569 --> 13:42.780
Why did you kill me in your mind?!

13:42.863 --> 13:44.448
<i>Saying I'm fat now was too far.</i>

13:51.038 --> 13:52.748
The guys in the research room said

13:52.831 --> 13:55.793
Lu should be in a cell
on the fourth level of the basement.

13:55.876 --> 13:56.710
<i>Let's hurry.</i>

13:57.336 --> 13:59.463
You were amazing in that fight earlier.

13:59.547 --> 14:01.632
You definitely are the strongest hit man.

14:01.715 --> 14:04.385
<i>Don't underestimate</i>
<i>the members of The Order.</i>

14:04.969 --> 14:07.304
That's the group you used to be in, right?

14:07.846 --> 14:09.390
Are they that good?

14:09.473 --> 14:12.142
<i>Of course, some better than others.</i>

14:13.227 --> 14:16.438
<i>But let's say one Order member</i>
<i>took on ten of you.</i>

14:16.522 --> 14:18.732
<i>It'd take six seconds to kill all ten.</i>

14:18.816 --> 14:21.235
<i>That's less than a second for each one!</i>

14:21.819 --> 14:24.655
And that Nagumo guy is in The Order too?

14:24.738 --> 14:27.157
He didn't look like he was that good.

14:27.241 --> 14:30.619
<i>If you ever meet an Order member,</i>
<i>you should just play dead.</i>

14:35.165 --> 14:36.792
Mr. Sakamoto!

14:38.043 --> 14:40.379
How frustrating.
We were just getting started.

14:40.504 --> 14:42.339
BASEMENT LEVEL FIVE
SERVICE CORRIDOR

14:42.423 --> 14:44.967
That. Being. Said.

14:45.050 --> 14:48.345
I have reliable allies on my side.

14:48.429 --> 14:49.263
Mr. Onigahara.

14:49.346 --> 14:50.264
LEADER, ONIGAHARA

14:50.347 --> 14:51.181
Mr. Takamido.

14:51.265 --> 14:52.224
LEADER, TAKAMIDO

14:53.267 --> 14:54.226
So…

14:55.144 --> 14:58.022
See? I told you, didn't I, Osaragi?

14:58.105 --> 15:00.232
We caught three big fish.

15:00.316 --> 15:02.735
This was the right place to run amok.

15:03.319 --> 15:04.486
Mr. Reindeer…

15:04.570 --> 15:06.280
The Order, I see.

15:06.780 --> 15:09.074
What would the JAA's lapdogs want with us?

15:09.158 --> 15:11.952
Has your owner not trained you?

15:12.036 --> 15:14.413
Now, now, cut us some slack.

15:14.914 --> 15:17.833
It's such a big facility, we got lost.

15:18.334 --> 15:19.793
I'm sorry to hear that.

15:20.336 --> 15:23.756
Please, let me personally see you out.

15:24.465 --> 15:26.550
While we're here,
let me ask you something.

15:26.634 --> 15:28.385
Is Slur here?

15:28.969 --> 15:30.721
If he is, we'd like to kill him.

15:31.263 --> 15:33.807
I don't know what you're talking about.

15:35.601 --> 15:36.936
Never mind, then.

15:37.811 --> 15:38.771
In any case,

15:39.313 --> 15:44.068
the acts of manufacturing illegal weapons
and coercion of hostages, among others,

15:44.151 --> 15:46.195
are against JAA regulations.

15:47.237 --> 15:49.323
Sorry, but we'll have to exterminate you.

15:51.575 --> 15:55.079
Oh, but could I nip to the loo first?

15:55.746 --> 15:56.789
Boss?

15:56.872 --> 15:58.749
Can we kill him?

15:58.832 --> 16:00.250
Too close, boys.

16:00.751 --> 16:04.672
Please do, Mr. Onigahara, Mr. Takamido.

16:04.755 --> 16:07.925
Are we done with them, Mr. Shishiba?

16:08.008 --> 16:09.718
Osaragi, let me--

16:17.309 --> 16:19.269
What? Weren't you done?

16:19.853 --> 16:22.398
I wanted to step away
because you always make a mess.

16:22.481 --> 16:23.399
Too late.

16:23.899 --> 16:25.150
Sorry.

16:25.234 --> 16:27.820
Don't get me wrong, I'm not angry.

16:27.903 --> 16:30.239
I am glad I wore my cheap suit, though.

16:30.322 --> 16:33.742
But are you sure that blood
wasn't there to begin with?

16:34.451 --> 16:36.412
That's a great way to lose friends.

16:39.039 --> 16:40.666
You two…

16:41.250 --> 16:44.169
don't recognize the value of human life.

16:44.253 --> 16:45.087
What?

16:45.587 --> 16:49.216
The people you've killed on a whim,
each and every one…

16:51.135 --> 16:54.722
may have had family and friends.

16:56.432 --> 16:58.934
Poor things. Those poor, poor things.

16:59.893 --> 17:02.354
I must kill you now.

17:05.399 --> 17:08.694
If you do not understand
how precious life is,

17:08.777 --> 17:11.363
you do not have the right to be hit men.

17:11.447 --> 17:15.617
Haven't they killed a lot of people too?

17:15.701 --> 17:19.872
Yet he thinks he's better than us.
Disgusting. Despicable.

17:19.955 --> 17:22.249
No doubt his boss is also a piece of sh--

17:28.756 --> 17:33.093
Everything I do is based on <i>his</i> wishes.

17:33.635 --> 17:37.056
Thus, the kills I perform are

17:37.139 --> 17:39.975
meaningful, acceptable acts.

17:40.476 --> 17:41.560
Really now?

17:44.021 --> 17:46.940
So it does have something to do with Slur.

17:47.024 --> 17:48.942
Mr. Shishiba, are you all right?

17:49.026 --> 17:51.528
Don't be ridiculous.
I was just testing the waters.

17:52.571 --> 17:54.740
You don't swing at the first pitch, see?

17:57.534 --> 17:59.453
Oh, sod off already.

17:59.536 --> 18:00.788
Forgive me.

18:00.871 --> 18:03.457
I have a man-made skeleton, you see.

18:07.669 --> 18:10.255
Hi there. Looking good, Mr. Saka.

18:10.964 --> 18:13.759
Long time no see, Shishiba.
How's everyone doing?

18:14.301 --> 18:16.011
You know, same old, same old.

18:16.553 --> 18:19.348
This is Osaragi, she's new.

18:19.431 --> 18:21.433
You haven't met her, have you, Mr. Saka?

18:22.309 --> 18:24.061
<i>He's like a teddy bear…</i>

18:24.686 --> 18:26.063
Sakamoto?

18:26.605 --> 18:29.066
You're the legendary hit man…

18:29.149 --> 18:30.692
Who's that?

18:30.776 --> 18:33.445
He's the boss of the group
that took over the Lab.

18:33.946 --> 18:35.572
He's as stubborn as a mule.

18:36.406 --> 18:39.451
The one person who wounded <i>him.</i>

18:39.535 --> 18:40.369
What?

18:40.452 --> 18:42.287
You know Slur?

18:43.163 --> 18:45.415
I don't know how you ended up here,

18:45.499 --> 18:49.128
but I must kill you immediately
and offer you to <i>him.</i>

18:49.795 --> 18:51.672
He's really disturbing.

18:52.923 --> 18:53.841
Okay, then.

18:55.884 --> 18:57.594
If you don't mind…

18:57.678 --> 19:00.472
This Weapon-man is pretty intense.

19:00.556 --> 19:02.599
Hmm? What's the matter, Osaragi?

19:08.355 --> 19:10.774
I gotta find Lu
and link back up with Mr. Sakamoto.

19:10.858 --> 19:12.568
We can't be late for dinner!

19:17.489 --> 19:18.448
You again!

19:18.532 --> 19:19.908
You invisible asshole!

19:20.784 --> 19:23.328
Man… It's so much easier
when I'm not noticed.

19:23.412 --> 19:24.454
LEADER, SEBA

19:24.538 --> 19:25.414
I guess this'll do.

19:26.582 --> 19:28.250
Lu better not be hurt.

19:28.834 --> 19:32.045
No clue. I just follow orders, man.

19:32.546 --> 19:34.923
I get a bonus if I kill you.

19:35.007 --> 19:37.176
Or wait, was I supposed to take you alive?

19:37.676 --> 19:38.510
Eh, whatever.

19:39.094 --> 19:41.054
I'm afraid I'll be going now.

19:41.138 --> 19:43.640
I don't have the time
to help boost your piggybank!

19:43.724 --> 19:47.394
I want to save up 20 million yen
before I hit retirement age.

19:47.477 --> 19:49.646
But I don't like working overtime.

19:49.730 --> 19:52.191
I'll be leaving work on time,
if you don't mind.

19:52.733 --> 19:53.901
<i>Let's get this over with.</i>

19:54.902 --> 19:56.195
<i>There he is!</i>

19:59.489 --> 20:00.574
<i>Shit.</i>

20:00.657 --> 20:03.410
<i>I can figure out where he is</i>
<i>by reading his mind,</i>

20:03.493 --> 20:06.246
<i>but that's useless if I can't see</i>
<i>how he's gonna attack.</i>

20:08.916 --> 20:09.750
Wait.

20:09.833 --> 20:14.296
I don't want to leave early either,
so don't make this too easy, okay?

20:17.716 --> 20:18.634
<i>Is he even…</i>

20:19.760 --> 20:20.844
<i>human?</i>

20:25.182 --> 20:29.519
We've got somewhere to be,
so we'll leave this to you.

20:29.603 --> 20:31.855
Okay. Say hi to the gang for me.

20:35.525 --> 20:38.445
Will Mr. Teddybear be okay without us?

20:38.528 --> 20:42.491
Sure. Our real target is Slur,
not that reindeer.

20:43.158 --> 20:46.161
Mr. Teddybear didn't look strong at all.

20:46.703 --> 20:48.664
I'm sure he'll die.

20:48.747 --> 20:53.418
If I'm being honest, that patchwork doll
did do better than I expected.

20:53.502 --> 20:55.629
He'll give Mr. Saka a run for his money.

20:56.255 --> 20:58.423
The thing is, I've known him for years,

20:58.507 --> 21:01.843
<i>and I just can't picture him ever dying.</i>

21:05.514 --> 21:08.600
This whole psychic thing is a drag.

21:08.684 --> 21:10.936
He keeps avoiding fatal hits, just barely.

21:11.561 --> 21:14.106
Fighting an invisible guy is way worse!

21:14.189 --> 21:18.151
Well, my shift's over soon,
so let's finish up.

21:28.495 --> 21:30.539
Aw man, that's gross.

21:32.874 --> 21:34.751
Can't miss now.

21:35.294 --> 21:36.795
What are you talking about?

21:44.678 --> 21:47.848
Look, Piisuke, an invisible man!

21:48.515 --> 21:51.143
Some people are really creative, huh?

21:52.477 --> 21:55.230
Perfect timing, Heisuke!

23:20.899 --> 23:25.904
Subtitle translation by: Yuka Kristi
